# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Reference documents — none of it is ours to redistribute
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The whole tree, not the two subdirectories that happened to exist when this
# was written: docs/vendor/ was added later for adapter datasheets (Silicon
# Labs, Microchip, FTDI) and would otherwise have been committed to the public
# repository on the next `git add -A`.
docs/
docs/standards/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Marketing material (not source — keep it out of git)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
docs/marketing/
# Matched by name anywhere, not just under docs/: the two articles this repo
# once tracked sat at the repository root, and `git add -A` would take any
# replacement straight back in. The account QR that ships with the manual
# (static/qrcode.jpg, CMIS2Customer/qrcode.jpg) is deliberately not matched.
公众号*
推广*
*推广文章*
*网盘*
baidu_qr*

